# Meyer2026_COSMOS3D_z7p9 upper limit
# Paper: Meyer et al. 2026, A&A 712, A16 (COSMOS-3D), doi:10.1051/0004-6361/202557671; arXiv:2510.11373 (v3 checked)
# Source: Appendix C, Table 3 (arXiv v3), z=7.9 block, logL = 42.2 row: N=1, <c>=0.01, "< 2.54 (2 sigma)".
# Redshift: 7.50 < z < 9.05; median z = 7.78, mean z = 7.90
# Line: [O III] lambda5008; bin width 0.2 dex
# Note: 2-sigma upper limit ("limits are at the 2 sigma level", Table 3 footnote). The table omits the minus sign
#   (typo, also in v2); the LF figure (fig_O3_LF) plots this bin at logPhi = -3.66 with a +0.56 dex upper error,
#   and -3.66 + 2x0.56 = -2.55, consistent with logPhi < -2.54. Average completeness is only 1%.
#
# Columns:
# Log10(L / erg s^-1)
# Log10(Phi_upper_limit / cMpc^-3 dex^-1)
#
42.2  -2.54
